    description: "Add a '--backend rust-analyzer' / '--backend tree-sitter' CLI flag to relevant hypergumbo commands (run, slice, sketch at minimum) that feeds into hypergumbo_lang_rust_analyzer.gate.should_use_rust_analyzer_backend. Today the backend activates only via the HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER environment variable; the gate already accepts a backend_flag kwarg, so the work is purely argparse plumbing.\n\nApproach:\n1. Add '--backend' argument to the common argparse parser (_build_parser or equivalent). Default None means 'use env var or tree-sitter'.\n2. Set HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 in os.environ when args.backend == 'rust-analyzer' (one-line side effect at CLI entry). OR thread the flag through to the analyzer registry so the analyzer layer can call should_use_rust_analyzer_backend(backend_flag=args.backend) directly.\n3. Tests: argparse accepts 'rust-analyzer' / 'tree-sitter' / None (default) / rejects other values; end-to-end test that --backend rust-analyzer triggers the backend (assert on a mock that try_analyze_with_rust_analyzer is called).\n\nBlocked by nothing — WI-duzul Slice C-final (merged 544d86983) delivered analyze_rust_with_scip which already consumes the gate; this item wires the CLI flag into that gate."  # 94ec
